Day 3 — GCP Networking + VPC + Load Balancing

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ You need multi-region application deployment with low latency. How would you design the VPC and network flow?

2️⃣ A VM in a private subnet cannot access the internet to install packages. What configuration changes will you make?

3️⃣ Your VPC is flat and resources can talk freely with each other. How will you enforce network segmentation & isolation?

4️⃣ You have 50+ VPCs across different GCP projects. How will you enable secure and scalable connectivity between them?

5️⃣ For hybrid connectivity between on-prem and GCP, when will you choose Cloud VPN vs Cloud Interconnect?

6️⃣ You want to expose only one internal service to a partner network without allowing VPC access. How will you achieve this?

7️⃣ You need to restrict access to a service based on specific geographic regions. How can this be implemented?

8️⃣ A service behind an internal load balancer must be accessible globally. How will you redesign the architecture?

9️⃣ What is the difference between HTTP(S) Load Balancer and TCP/UDP Load Balancer? When do you use which?

🔟 Your application requires SSL termination + URL-based routing + autoscaling backend support. Which load balancer fits best?

